{"id": "c10", "kind": "web", "text": "표의 Claude 값은 max effort, Terminal-Bench 4.0 만 xhigh, 안전장치 개입 시 cyber 는 Opus 4.8, 생물학·frontier LLM 개발은 Opus 5 가 풀었다 (06장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "w1 §Performance 표 설명문", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance · table note", "quote": "Unless otherwise noted, all Claude Opus 5.5 results use adaptive thinking at max effort. Terminal-Bench 4.0 results are reported for Claude Opus 5.5 at xhigh effort and GPT-6 Astra at high effort, as reported by OpenAI; these represent each model’s highest score. Claude Opus 5.5 was evaluated with its production safeguards enabled. When they intervened, cybersecurity tasks were completed by Claude Opus 4.8, and biology and frontier LLM development tasks were completed by Claude Opus 5."}]}
{"id": "c11", "kind": "numeric", "text": "Terminal-Bench 표준오차 ±2.6pt(Opus 5.5)·±1.6~2pt(다른 Claude), 리더보드 Opus 5 51.8% 대 재현 52.3%; TB-Science ±3.5~5pt, 30.0% 대 29.0% (05장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "w1 각주 1·3", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance · footnote 1", "quote": "The standard error is ±2.6 pts for Claude Opus 5.5 and ±1.6–2 pts for the other Claude models. The public leaderboard (5 trials/task, Claude Code harness) reports Claude Opus 5 at 51.8%; our setup reproduces it at 52.3%, within noise."}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance · footnote 3", "quote": "The standard error is ±3.5–5 pts per model. The public leaderboard (3 trials/task, Claude Code harness) reports Claude Opus 5 at 30.0%; our setup reproduces it at 29.0%, within noise."}]}
{"id": "c12", "kind": "web", "text": "AutomationBench 는 Zapier 가 fallback 없이 돌려 안전장치 개입을 실패로 쳤고 실제보다 낮다고 원문이 쓴다 (05·11장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "w1 각주 2", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance · footnote 2", "quote": "These runs were performed without fallback models, so safeguard interventions were considered failures—this resulted in a lower score than Claude Opus 5.5 would achieve in practice."}]}
{"id": "c13", "kind": "web", "text": "Anthropic 이 실제 사용에서 Fable 5.1 과의 격차는 점수가 시사하는 것보다 좁다고 적었다 (02·06·21장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "w1 §Performance ¶1", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance and cost-effectiveness ¶1", "quote": "at these levels of capability we’ve found that benchmark margins have become a less reliable guide to real-world differences. In our own use, the gap between Opus 5.5 and Claude Fable 5.1 is narrower than these scores suggest."}]}
{"id": "c14", "kind": "numeric", "text": "시스템 카드 §8.4: 각 모델 최고 effort 기준 FrontierCode Main 은 Opus 5.5 54.6%, Opus 5 53.4%, GPT-6 Astra 53.3%, Fable 5.1 52.8% (06장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "s1 §8.4 p.176", "evidence": [{"source": "s1", "locator": "§8.4 p.176", "quote": "Opus 5.5 ranks first on FrontierCode (Main) with a 54.6% score (each model at its best reasoning effort), improving on Claude Opus 5 (53.4%) and leading Claude Fable 5 (53.5%), GPT-6 Astra (53.3%), and Claude Fable 5.1 (52.8%)."}]}
{"id": "c15", "kind": "derived", "text": "표 기준 FrontierCode 의 Opus 5 와의 격차 6.4pt(54.4−48.0)가 각 모델 최고 effort 기준으로는 1.2pt(54.6−53.4)다 (06·21·23장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "원문 표와 시스템 카드 §8.4 대조", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance · table", "quote": "Agentic codingFrontierCode v1.1 (Main)54.4%50.3%48.0%53.3%47.5%"}, {"source": "s1", "locator": "§8.4 p.176", "quote": "Opus 5.5 ranks first on FrontierCode (Main) with a 54.6% score (each model at its best reasoning effort), improving on Claude Opus 5 (53.4%)"}], "derived_from": ["w1 표: 54.4 vs 48.0", "s1 §8.4: 54.6 vs 53.4"], "note": "두 기준을 나란히 놓은 비교는 어느 문서에도 없다. Opus 5 의 최고점 53.4 는 원문 차트의 med 점, Fable 5.1 의 52.8 은 low 점과 일치한다"}
{"id": "c16", "kind": "web", "text": "시스템 카드는 FrontierCode 점수가 medium 위에서 내려가며 그 이유를 범위 밖 변경을 감점하는 채점에서 찾는다 (06장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "s1 §8.4 p.176 note", "evidence": [{"source": "s1", "locator": "§8.4 p.176 note", "quote": "There is a decline in model performance on FrontierCode (Main and Extended) above medium effort. The evaluation is designed around writing mergeable code diffs without requiring human edits, so its grading penalizes out-of-scope changes that may be unnecessary, even if they are high quality or helpful."}]}
